This project builds on the following third-party work. Each part keeps its own licence.

* Intrinsic Core (https://github.com/intrinsic-ai/intrinsic-core), Apache-2.0: the world model, motion planner,
  real-time control (ICON) and grasp planning services the robot stack runs. Built from source into one container;
  the generated gRPC stubs in gen/intrinsic/ come from its protos.
* NVIDIA Isaac Sim 5.1: the physics simulator. It is not redistributed; install it separately under NVIDIA's terms.
* Franka Panda robot model (franka_description by Franka Emika GmbH, via Isaac Sim), Apache-2.0: see
  assets/robots/franka/LICENSE.md.
* ROS 2 Humble and MoveIt 2: the bridge between Isaac Sim and the robot service, and the grasp planner. Installed
  in the container from the ROS apt repositories under their own licences (Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause).
* intrinsic-moveit (https://github.com/intrinsic-ai/intrinsic-moveit), tag v0.0.4, Apache-2.0: the grasp planning
  sources vendored in ros_ws/src/ (moveit_planning_interfaces, grasp_planner), with the changes listed in
  ros_ws/src/VENDORED.md.
* moveit_resources Panda MoveIt config (ros-humble-moveit-resources-panda-moveit-config), BSD-3-Clause: the
  collision exemptions and OMPL settings in ros_ws/src/franka_grasp_config/.
* tinygltf (third_party/tinygltf), MIT.
* Muse Glimmer 30B (meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B), Apache-2.0: the base model of the published adapters. The
  fine-tuning recipe and evaluation path follow the Meta model cookbook (Apache-2.0).
* Muse Spark and Muse Wonder (Meta Model API), Muse Voice Transcribe: used as hosted services; their terms apply.
